WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.830
A lumber merchant's son once written off as too dull for business, Fischer became

2
00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:12.390
the most exacting organic chemist in Germany by reading structure off behavior.

3
00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:18.573
Through the 1880s and 1890s he wrestled the sugars into order using osazones,

4
00:00:18.793 --> 00:00:24.213
oxidation, and the cyanohydrin chain extension, deducing which hydroxyl pointed

5
00:00:24.213 --> 00:00:27.473
which way long before any instrument could see a molecule.

6
00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:32.707
The Fischer projection you will draw in this chapter is the notation he invented to

7
00:00:32.707 --> 00:00:36.807
keep that three-dimensional bookkeeping straight on flat paper, and the D .L.

8
00:00:37.207 --> 00:00:38.207
convention is his.

9
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.380
From the same work came his "lock and key" image of enzyme specificity the idea that

10
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:49.460
a protein and its sugar must fit together geometrically which is exactly the

11
00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.140
principle the lectins at the end of this lesson run on.

12
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.640
The phenylhydrazine that let him fingerprint the sugars also, slowly, poisoned him;

13
00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.380
he died in 1919.
